      {
        "_id": "wcHvgTraits00001",
        "effects": [],
        "flags": {},
        "folder": null,
        "img": "icons/svg/aura.svg",
        "name": "Construct Traits",
        "ownership": {
          "default": 0
        },
        "sort": 0,
        "system": {
          "abilityType": "nat",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>The harvest golem is a mindless construct with d10 Hit Dice, three-quarter base attack progression, no good saves, no skill points or feats, and no Stamina or Intellect score. It has darkvision 60 feet and low-light vision. It is proficient with its natural weapons; a humanoid-shaped construct is also proficient with weapons named in its entry. It is not proficient with armor.</p><p>It is immune to mind-affecting effects, poison, sleep, paralysis, stunning, disease, death effects, necromancy effects, fatigue, exhaustion, energy drain, ability damage, and ability drain. It is not subject to critical hits or nonlethal damage and is immune to effects requiring a Fortitude save unless they also affect objects or are harmless.</p><p>It is destroyed at 0 hit points, cannot heal damage naturally, and cannot be raised or resurrected. It can be repaired by suitable magic or the Craft Construct feat, and fast healing still functions if it gains that quality. It is not subject to massive damage and does not eat, sleep, or breathe. A Medium construct gains 20 bonus hit points.</p><p><strong>Foundry:</strong> the absent abilities, +20 hit points, common condition immunities, 100% fortification, and destruction at 0 hit points are represented in the actor data. Adjudicate the Fortitude-save and object-affecting exceptions from this feature.</p>"
          },
          "featType": "trait",
          "senses": {
            "darkvision": 60,
            "lowLight": true,
            "lowLightMultiplier": 2
          },
          "source": "World of Warcraft: Monster Guide, p. 187",
          "uniqueId": "wc-harvest-golem-construct-traits"
        },
        "type": "feat"
      }
    ]
