      "alignment": "Always neutral",
      "biography": {
        "public": "",
        "value": "<h2>Harvest Golem</h2><p>A harvest golem looks like a common field scarecrow until its hidden face and long dagger-fingers reveal it as an unnaturally swift guardian. Goblin tinkers first built these constructs to patrol Westfall, and their brutal efficiency allowed the design to spread far beyond those fields.</p><p>The golem is mindless but possesses enough innate cunning to vary its tactics. It never retreats.</p>"
      },
      "cr": 5,
      "environment": "Any",
      "level": {
        "available": 0,
        "max": 15,
        "min": 7,
        "value": 7
      },
      "notes": {
        "public": "",
        "value": "<h2>Profile</h2><p><strong>Area:</strong> Westfall. <strong>Organization:</strong> solitary. <strong>Treasure:</strong> special. <strong>Advancement:</strong> 8-15 HD (Medium). <strong>Level adjustment:</strong> none.</p><h2>Combat</h2><p>The golem remains still and relies on Lifeless Mien until creatures enter its 20-foot partial-charge range. It then charges the nearest suitable target and uses Backstab. It can make one keen claw attack as a standard action or two keen claw attacks as a full attack. Though mindless, it can vary its tactics somewhat and never retreats.</p><h2>Treasure</h2><p>A destroyed harvest golem yields eight claw blades. They lose their +1 keen magic but remain masterwork daggers. Other creatures take a -2 attack penalty when using them, resulting in a net -1 after the masterwork bonus. Each usually sells for no more than 100 gp.</p><h2>Construction</h2><p>The body requires 500 gp of special powders and herbs plus powdered arcanite ink for its runes. Construction costs 2,500 gp per Hit Die and requires a DC 15 Craft (tailoring) check.</p><p><strong>Requirements:</strong> caster level 6th; Craft Construct; <em>bladestorm</em>, <em>geas/quest</em>, and <em>limited wish</em>. <strong>Price:</strong> 18,000 gp. <strong>Cost:</strong> 9,250 gp plus 1,000 XP.</p><p><strong>Source:</strong> <em>World of Warcraft: Monster Guide</em>, printed pages 85-86.</p>"
      },
      "totalCr": 5,
      "type": "Construct"
    },
